This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor two sensors on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It sets up GPIO4 for the flame sensor with an internal pull-up resistor and registers a falling-edge ISR to debounce the flame sensor. The temperature sensor is connected to an ADS1115 ADC on I2C bus 1, and the program reads the temperature every 100ms. If both a debounced flame event and temperature above 60°C occur together, it logs the event with a timestamp and sounds the buzzer for 2 seconds. If only flame is detected, it logs "Flame detected!"; if only the temperature exceeds 60°C, it logs the temperature reading. The program handles errors and releases resources on all exit paths.

