This C program interfaces with a Melexis MLX91211 Triaxis Current Sensor using an MCP3008 ADC connected over hardware SPI0 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It logs current readings in Amperes to a `current_log.csv` file and simulates an overcurrent safety system for a DC motor. The program uses the `libgpiod` API for GPIO control and `spidev` for SPI communication with the MCP3008. It samples the sensor every 1 second, converts the 10-bit ADC value to a voltage, then to current using a sensitivity of 0.1 V/A and an offset of 0.05V. If the current exceeds 10.0A, it drives a motor shutdown pin (GPIO17) LOW to disable the motor, logs the event, waits 1 second, then drives it HIGH to re-enable. It checks all open(), ioctl(), read(), and file I/O operations for errors, and retries SPI communication errors up to 3 times. Signal handling (SIGINT, SIGTERM) is implemented for graceful shutdown, closing all file descriptors and releasing GPIO lines cleanly on exit.

