This C program initializes the pigpio library, opens the SPI channel, and continuously samples the ADC connected to the microphone amplifier. It calculates an exponential moving average (EMA) of the readings and logs a peak whenever the raw value exceeds the EMA by a dynamic threshold margin of 20%. The program handles pigpio initialization errors, SPI communication failures, and log file I/O errors. It also gracefully shuts down on SIGINT/SIGTERM by releasing all resources.

