This C program continuously monitors the AIN0 analog input channel of a PCF8591 ADC connected to the Raspberry Pi at I2C address 0x48 on bus `/dev/i2c-1`. It uses `libgpiod` for GPIO needs (though none are used in this specific example) and `i2c-dev` for I2C communication. The program initializes the I2C bus, configures the ADC for single-ended mode on channel 0, performs a dummy read to discard the previous conversion result, and then continuously reads and prints the current sample value every 100 ms. It handles errors by checking every I2C `ioctl`, `read`, and `write` call and exits with a non-zero code on failure. It also handles `SIGINT` (Ctrl-C) by closing the I2C file descriptor before exiting.

