This code sets up a Theremin-like instrument using libgpiod for GPIO control and the sysfs PWM interface for audio generation. It reads distance from an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor and maps it to an audio frequency, and controls the volume using a photoresistor read via an MCP3008 ADC over SPI0. It handles sensor read errors gracefully, manages all resources cleanly on SIGINT, and saves and loads calibration data to 'theremin_config.txt'.

