This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor an MQ-135 air quality sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC over SPI. It reads the ADC value every 5 seconds, converts it to an AQI, and controls a ventilation fan connected to GPIO18 based on the AQI threshold. It logs the timestamp and AQI to 'air_quality.log' and handles errors, retries, and graceful shutdown.

