This C program reads analog voltage from an MQ-3 alcohol sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI0 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It uses the libgpiod library for GPIO control and the standard Linux spidev for SPI communication. The program logs readings to 'alcohol_log.txt' with ISO 8601 UTC timestamps, classifies readings based on PPM values, and handles ADC read errors robustly. It also gracefully handles SIGINT/SIGTERM signals for shutdown.

