    while (1) {
        distance = read_distance();
        if (distance < 0) {
            continue;
        }

        now = time(NULL);
        log_file = fopen(LOG_FILE, "a");
        if (log_file == NULL) {
            perror("Error opening log file");
            continue;
        }

        fprintf(log_file, "%s %.2f mm\n", ctime(&now), distance);
        fclose(log_file);

        if (distance < DISTANCE_THRESHOLD) {
            printf("Feeder Activated\n");
        } else {
            printf("Feeder Idle\n");
        }

        sleep(1);
    }

    return 0;
}
```

This C program reads the digital input from GPIO 17, converts it to a placeholder voltage, calculates the distance, logs the reading with a timestamp, and checks if the distance is below the threshold to activate the feeder. It handles errors gracefully and unexports GPIO 17 on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

