This C program captures an MJPEG video stream from a USB webcam connected at `/dev/video0` on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It configures the video capture for a resolution of 640x480 using the V4L2 API directly. For every captured frame, it logs the timestamp in microseconds to a file named `frame_log.txt`. The program uses memory-mapped (MMAP) buffers for frame capture and handles input and output asynchronously with `select()` to avoid blocking indefinitely. It includes robust error handling for every V4L2 `ioctl` call, every file operation, and every memory mapping, ensuring clean resource release on all exit paths, including a graceful shutdown triggered by `SIGINT`.

