This C program captures video from the CSI camera on a Raspberry Pi 4, streams it over UDP to a specified server IP and port, and handles errors at every syscall. It uses V4L2 MMAP streaming with 4 buffers at 640x480 YUYV format. Each frame is fragmented into UDP datagrams of at most 65000 bytes, with a small header containing frame index, fragment index, total fragment count, and payload size. The program runs until SIGINT or SIGTERM is received, then cleanly stops streaming, unmaps all buffers, and closes all descriptors.

