This C program uses the libgpiod library to control a camera pan-tilt system with two hobby servos on a Raspberry Pi. It sets up GPIO lines for the servos and buttons, initializes them with the correct settings, and enters a loop where it polls the buttons every 50 ms, adjusting the servo positions accordingly. The program handles errors and cleans up resources when SIGINT is received.

