This C program uses the libgpiod library to control an HC-SR04 ultrasonic distance sensor on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It sets up GPIO 17 as the trigger pin and GPIO 27 as the echo pin, with a voltage divider to protect the Pi's 3.3V GPIO from the 5V logic output of the sensor. It generates a 10 microsecond trigger pulse, measures the echo pulse width using libgpiod edge events, and calculates the distance. It logs every measurement, including errors and timeouts, with an ISO-8601 timestamp to 'distance_log.txt'. If the distance is below 15 cm, it logs a 'Time to water the plant!' reminder. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, releasing all libgpiod resources and closing the log file.

