This C program initializes the pigpio library, sets up a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and continuously reads distance measurements from the TDK Chirp ICU-20201 Ultrasonic Time-of-Flight sensor over I2C bus 1. It logs each reading with an ISO 8601 timestamp to 'distance_log.txt' and triggers a GPIO alert on physical pin 17 (BCM 17) if the distance falls below 10.0 cm. It handles I2C read/write errors, sensor absence, and log file creation errors. The main loop checks for a signal-requested shutdown before each sample, ensuring no partial or corrupted log line is ever produced. On SIGINT/SIGTERM, it cleanly releases all resources -- I2C handles, GPIO, and pigpio.

