This C program initializes the pigpio library, sets up the GPIO pins for the ultrasonic sensor and buzzer, and registers an alert function for the echo pin. It sends a 10 microsecond HIGH trigger pulse and measures the echo pulse width to calculate the distance. The program handles pigpio initialization, GPIO mode configuration, and alert registration errors. It also correctly handles the 32-bit tick wraparound and reports invalid readings and sensor-absent conditions. The buzzer is activated when the distance is less than 30 cm and turned off once the distance returns to 30 cm or above. On SIGINT, the program performs a clean shutdown by turning off the buzzer and calling `gpioTerminate()`.

