This code sets up a smart parking gate system using the pigpio library for GPIO, PWM, and I2C operations. It initializes the VL53L1X sensor, sets up the GPIO pins, and continuously reads the distance from the sensor. The gate opens when an object is detected within 50 cm and closes when the distance exceeds 60 cm, with hysteresis to prevent rapid state changes. All gate state changes are logged to 'parking_log.txt' with timestamps and distances. The program handles errors and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths via SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handlers.

