This C program initializes the VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor using the pigpio library and reads distance measurements every 50 ms. It stores the last 10 readings in a circular buffer and activates a warning LED (connected to GPIO17) if any reading falls below 200 mm. The program installs a SIGINT handler to turn off the LED, close the I2C handle, and terminate pigpio on interrupt signals. It checks every I2C read/write operation and handles sensor initialization failures.

