This C program initializes the pigpio library, opens the I2C bus, and sets up a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM. It then enters a loop where it sends a trigger command to the SDP31 sensor, waits 1 ms, reads the data, converts the raw pressure and temperature values, logs them to a file, and repeats every 100 ms. If an I2C operation fails, it retries with exponential backoff. On receiving a SIGINT or SIGTERM, it sets the `exit_flag` to 1, allowing the loop to exit cleanly. On exit, it closes the log file, closes the I2C handle, and terminates the pigpio library.

