This C program uses the pigpio library to interface with a Si7021 humidity and temperature sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x40. It reads temperature and humidity every 2 seconds, logs the readings with a timestamp into a 60-entry circular buffer, and prints it to stdout. It controls a cooling fan on GPIO18 (active-high) based on the temperature readings, turning the fan ON when the temperature exceeds 28.0 °C and OFF when it falls below 27.0 °C. The program handles SIGINT by turning off the fan, closing the I2C handle, and calling `gpioTerminate()` before exiting.

