This C program uses the `pigpio` library to bit-bang the single-wire protocol of a DHT11 temperature/humidity sensor connected to GPIO 4 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It includes error handling for timeouts, checksum failures, and sensor-absent conditions. It logs temperature and humidity readings to `dht11_readings.txt` with ISO-8601 timestamps and logs errors with timestamps and status codes to the standard error. On receiving a SIGINT or SIGTERM, it releases GPIO resources, calls `gpioTerminate()`, and closes any open file handles before exiting.

