This C program reads data from a TDK ICP-10125 barometric pressure sensor over I2C, drives a warning LED using libgpiod, and handles errors and resource cleanup. It reads calibration coefficients, triggers measurements, reads pressure and temperature data, verifies the CRC, and applies conversion formulas to compute pressure and temperature. The LED blinks at different frequencies based on the pressure reading. The program handles SIGINT to release the GPIO line and close the I2C file descriptor cleanly.

