This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to read temperature and pressure from a BMP180 sensor connected over I2C bus 1. It uses the pigpio library to configure GPIO2 as a falling-edge triggered interrupt to toggle data logging on and off. The main loop polls every second to read and log the timestamped temperature and pressure readings to `altitude_log.txt` in CSV format. It handles I2C read and write errors, verifies the calibration data, and ensures graceful exit on SIGINT by closing the I2C handle, closing the file, and releasing the GPIO.

