This C program reads temperature from a MAX31865 RTD-to-digital converter over SPI0 on a Raspberry Pi 5, logs the readings with timestamps to `rtd_log.csv`, and handles errors gracefully. It uses the `libgpiod` library for chip-select line management and the standard Linux `spidev` interface for SPI communication. The program initializes the MAX31865 for 3-wire RTD mode with bias voltage enabled, reads the RTD registers, checks the fault status register, and calculates temperature using the Callendar-Van Dusen equation. It also implements robust error handling for SPI communication failures and sensor read errors, and handles sensor-absent and SPI bus-error paths by logging errors without crashing. The program implements graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM, properly closing the SPI device file descriptor and the log file.

