This C program initializes the pigpio library and opens the I2C device for the BMP180 pressure sensor. It reads the calibration data from the sensor and sets up a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM to clean up resources. The program toggles logging based on a falling edge detected on GPIO27, with a 200 ms debounce delay. When logging is enabled, it reads the pressure from the sensor, calculates the pressure using the Bosch compensation formulas, and writes the timestamp and pressure to a file named `pressure_log.txt` every 2 seconds.

