This C program uses the pigpio library to control a solid-state relay on GPIO17 to modulate a resistive heater. It reads the temperature from a MAX31855 thermocouple amplifier over the hardware SPI peripheral (SPI0) and implements a PI controller with anti-windup to maintain a target temperature. The program logs temperature and PWM duty cycle to `heater_log.csv` with ISO-8601 timestamps. It handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, ensuring the heater is turned off, SPI is closed, the log file is closed, and pigpio is terminated. The target temperature defaults to 25.0°C, and the maximum duty cycle is set to 80% to prevent overheating.

