This C program uses the pigpio library to toggle data logging from a BMP180 pressure sensor based on a push-button interrupt on GPIO4. It reads the BMP180 calibration coefficients at startup, validates them, and logs pressure readings in hPa to `pressure_log.txt` with timestamps. The program uses a falling-edge ISR on GPIO4 with an internal pull-up to toggle logging on and off, debouncing in the ISR using pigpio tick comparison. It reads the BMP180 pressure with oversampling OSS=3 and implements the full Bosch BMP180 compensation algorithm using integer arithmetic. The program samples every 2 seconds and handles SIGINT cleanly by closing the I2C handle and releasing pigpio resources before exiting. It checks every I2C read/write return value and reports errors to stderr.

