This C program uses the libgpiod v1 API to monitor a capacitive touch sensor connected to GPIO 17 on a Raspberry Pi 5. It opens `gpiochip0` by name, requests the line as input with the consumer label "ttp223_tamper", and polls the line every 100 ms using `CLOCK_MONOTONIC`. If the sensor remains continuously touched for more than 5 seconds, it prints an intrusion alert to stdout once per touch event and resets the timer when the sensor is released. It checks every libgpiod call for failure and prints `strerror(errno)` on error. It handles `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` for graceful shutdown, releasing the line and closing the chip on all exit paths.

