This C program initializes the ALSA PCM device for capturing audio data from the INMP441 I2S MEMS microphone, sets up the GPIO line to select the left channel, and continuously reads 32-bit frames from the PCM device. It extracts the 24-bit data, right-shifts it to produce 16-bit PCM samples, and writes these samples to a raw file named 'audio_capture.pcm'. The program handles errors robustly and releases resources on all exit paths, including when a SIGINT (Ctrl+C) is received.

