This C program reads capacitive touch events from a TTP223 touch sensor connected to GPIO4 (physical pin 7) on a Raspberry Pi 5. It uses the libgpiod library to configure the GPIO line as an input with a pull-down bias and polls the line with a debounce interval of approximately 50 ms. On every press or release transition, it appends a line to the 'touch_log.txt' file in the specified format and flushes the file after each write. It verifies every libgpiod call and prints a diagnostic to stderr on failure. If the log file cannot be opened, it releases all GPIO resources before exiting with a non-zero status. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown by releasing the line, closing the chip, closing the log file, and exiting cleanly.

