This C program uses the libgpiod API to monitor two Omron D7E-5 tilt sensors connected to GPIO lines 17 and 18 on a Raspberry Pi 5. It configures both lines as inputs with an active-low pull-up, polls them every 100 ms, and uses edge detection with a 50 ms debounce window to avoid duplicate logs. When a line transitions from inactive (1) to active (0), it logs a timestamped event to `/var/log/tilt_events.log`. The program handles chip-open failure, line-request failure, and read errors by printing a message to stderr and exiting or continuing gracefully. It also installs handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to release all libgpiod resources and close the log file cleanly before exiting.

