This C program reads tri-axial acceleration data from an LSM303D accelerometer/magnetometer connected via I2C on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It uses the Linux i2c-dev kernel API for I2C communication and the libgpiod library for GPIO interrupt line request and event monitoring. The program initializes the device, configures the accelerometer, sets up an interrupt on GPIO23, and continuously polls acceleration data at 10 ms intervals, storing samples in a circular buffer. On a rising edge of the INT1 GPIO interrupt, it prints a timestamp and dumps the last 10 buffered samples. The program handles errors, SIGINT (Ctrl-C) gracefully, and releases resources on all exit paths.

