This C program reads an SW-420 vibration sensor's active-high digital output on GPIO17 (physical pin 11) using the libgpiod API. It polls for both rising and falling edges with a timeout specified by the user (default 1000 ms). It logs every edge event with an ISO-8601 timestamp and the raw value (0 or 1) to `vibration_events.log`, handling file open/write errors gracefully. It maintains a sliding window of the last 5 events and prints an EARTHQUAKE ALERT message to the console if 3 or more of them read HIGH. It checks every libgpiod call and syscall for errors, printing diagnostics to stderr. It installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler that sets a volatile `sig_atomic_t` flag so the main loop exits cleanly, releasing the line and closing the log file.

