This C program initializes the pigpio library and sets up GPIO pins for the touch sensor and relay. It sets up an interrupt handler for the touch sensor and toggles the relay state when the sensor is touched, with a debounce delay of 50 ms. The program runs indefinitely until terminated by a SIGINT (Ctrl+C) or SIGTERM signal. It handles errors during initialization and GPIO operations, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths.

