This C program uses the pigpio library to read magnetic field data from a Silicon Labs Si7210 Hall effect sensor over I2C bus 1 at its default address 0x30. It triggers a relay on GPIO 17 (active high) when the field strength exceeds a 5.0 mT threshold, sampling every 100 ms. It handles errors, checks every pigpio call, and releases resources on all exit paths. It also appends timestamped entries in ISO 8601 format to `magnetic_events.txt` for every field reading, relay state change, and error. A SIGINT handler is installed to close the I2C handle, deactivate the relay, terminate pigpio, and log the shutdown.

