This C program initializes the pigpio library and the MPR121 capacitive touch sensor on the Raspberry Pi 5. It sets up the GPIO relay on GPIO17 and configures the MPR121 with the specified parameters. It reads the touch status from the sensor and toggles the relay only on a fresh (rising-edge) touch of electrode 0, with a 200 ms debounce. The program handles errors for every pigpio/I2C call and ensures clean resource release on every exit path via SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. The relay is set to a known OFF state on both startup and shutdown.

