This C program sets up a TCP server on port 5000 to control a servo motor (connected to GPIO17) and read a PIR sensor (connected to GPIO4) on a Raspberry Pi 5. It uses the libgpiod API for GPIO operations and handles errors, logging, and graceful shutdown. The program listens for commands 'SERVO <angle>' and 'PIR', and logs all events to syslog and a local file named `security.log`.

