This C program initializes the pigpio library and sets up GPIO 4 as an input for the touch sensor and GPIO 17 as an output for the relay. It implements software debouncing with a 50 ms delay and toggles the relay state only when the touch sensor reads HIGH both before and after the delay. It waits for the touch sensor to return LOW before allowing the next toggle. The program logs every relay state change to the console with an ISO-8601 timestamp and the new state (ON/OFF). It handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for graceful shutdown by turning the relay OFF, releasing pigpio resources, and printing an exit message. It checks the return value of every pigpio call and reports errors to stderr. The main loop includes a 10 ms sleep to reduce CPU usage.

