This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor a Seeed Studio Grove Rain Sensor connected to GPIO4 (BCM) and controls an L298N motor driver connected to GPIO17, GPIO18, and GPIO27. It checks for rain every 60 seconds, debounces the sensor by taking 5 readings at 50 ms intervals, and treats rain as detected when at least 3 readings are LOW. When rain is detected, it logs the event, closes the window by driving the motor for 5 seconds, and logs the action. It waits 60 seconds before checking again. On SIGINT or SIGTERM, it stops the motor, releases GPIO resources, and closes the log before exiting.

